title: Coordinate the Press
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: press_coordination_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; press_coordination_timer += 4

= Coordinate the Press

Friendly newspapers can repeat a common message or preserve space for arguments
within the emerging coalition.

- @election_message: Concentrate on electoral integrity
- @coalition_debate: Publish the coalition's internal debate

@election_message
on-arrival: public_mandate += 5; constitutional_legitimacy += 3; court_relation -= 2
go-to: post_event

The coalition's public message emphasizes its demand for representative
elections.

@coalition_debate
on-arrival: coalition_cohesion += 2; political_intelligence += 3; public_mandate += 2
go-to: post_event

Publishing competing arguments makes the coalition look less unified, but helps
its members understand the choices ahead.
